from writer_late import Writer,B,G

w=Writer('2025-08-26'); p=w.price; Q=w.q

def macro():
    return [
    G('US','Mixed','policy opening / credibility risk',[
    ['Macro Stance',Q('n8363','CNBC reported that markets were confident about a September rate cut but much less certain about the path after it.')+' That is a more demanding setup than a simple policy-relief rally. The immediate benefit of cheaper money has to be balanced against weaker hiring, tariff costs and uncertainty about the institutions setting the price of money. Keep a constructive core allocation, but stop short of treating every pullback as an automatic invitation to add risk. A broad recovery needs companies to keep earning, banks to keep lending and investors to trust that inflation will be contained. If any of those links weakens, a lower expected policy rate can lose much of its appeal.'],
    ['Rates & Curve',w.treasury()+' '+p('^GSPC',(1,20))+' '+p('^VIX',(1,))+' '+p('DX-Y.NYB',(1,))+' The combination argues for discipline. Equity volatility remains contained, while the dollar’s rebound and firmer yields show that the adjustment to policy expectations is not a straight line. A modest pullback does not invalidate the broadening case, but it makes the next confirmation more valuable. Do not add leverage on the assumption that a central-bank speech permanently removed financing risk.'],
    ['New / Most Important',Q('n8383','NPR reported Trump seeking to remove Federal Reserve governor Lisa Cook, with a legal fight looming.')+' Treat the attempted removal as an institutional-risk event, with the outcome unresolved. Pressure for easier policy can lower expected short rates while increasing concern about inflation credibility and the compensation demanded to hold longer debt. Those channels can pull in opposite directions. The practical issue is whether a benign easing narrative becomes a more difficult discussion about policy independence and the long-run value of money. That risk favours diversification across operating cash flow, liquid duration and a measured hedge.'],
    ['Playbook ✓','Hold profitable companies through the pullback, but stage any cyclical additions and keep event-sensitive positions smaller. Add domestic breadth when credit and company guidance confirm that growth is surviving. Reduce if a stronger dollar, weaker credit and pressure on policy credibility arrive together. The mixed stance can improve when the market absorbs political uncertainty without a rise in long-term financing costs; it should become more defensive if falling short-rate expectations no longer support either credit or earnings. Avoid making the entire portfolio depend on a particular legal or political outcome.']]),
    G('EU','Mixed','activity improves / fiscal questions',[
    ['Macro Stance',Q('n3184','Le Monde reported French prime minister François Bayrou planning a confidence vote.')+' That adds a political and fiscal test to an economy where activity has shown signs of improvement. A recovery in customer demand and uncertainty about public financing can coexist. Investors should distinguish businesses with firm commercial orders from assets whose valuation depends heavily on an uninterrupted decline in government borrowing costs. Maintain selective exposure rather than treating the region as a uniform policy trade.'],
    ['Activity & Inflation',Q('n1305','S&P Global reported an improved August eurozone flash PMI, with manufacturing conditions moving forward.')+' '+p('^STOXX',(1,20))+' A stronger survey offers a better starting point for earnings, but order conversion and margin discipline remain the confirmation. Retailers and service companies face their own wage and input costs. Exporters also carry currency and tariff risks. A diversified allocation can therefore be sensible even when the index’s near-term direction looks indecisive.'],
    ['New / Most Important',Q('n4020','Politico examined the tension between the US trade agreement and Europe’s image as a defender of rules-based trade.')+' Policy predictability is economically valuable, yet the distribution of costs and benefits still matters. Firms need clarity about the rules that govern sourcing, sales and investment. A politically acceptable settlement is not necessarily equally favourable to every industry or member state. Keep earnings assumptions tied to company exposure rather than to the emotional tone of negotiation coverage.'],
    ['Playbook ✓','Prefer resilient domestic earnings and strong balance sheets, with a smaller allocation to exporters whose order books justify the risk. Watch the interaction between sovereign financing and private credit rather than assuming that lower policy rates will reach every borrower equally. Add regional beta when better activity produces credible profit revisions; trim if fiscal uncertainty raises financing costs while customer demand loses momentum. A selective portfolio can participate in improving demand without requiring an optimistic resolution of every political question.']]),
    G('CN','Mixed','savings rotate / real demand lags',[
    ['Macro Stance',Q('n1552','CNBC described Chinese household savings helping to fuel a stock-market boom.')+' The important investment question is where that money goes after it leaves a bank account. Buying existing shares can improve sentiment and lower the cost of equity without immediately creating household consumption or business investment. That distinction explains how a strong market can coexist with a subdued economy. Participate through liquid businesses with credible earnings, but resist the temptation to treat rising stock prices as proof that every domestic-demand problem has been solved. A rally funded by a reallocation of savings needs a second stage in which companies deliver more cash to shareholders.'],
    ['PMIs & Activity',Q('n0679','Global Times reported the July manufacturing PMI edging lower, citing the National Bureau of Statistics.')+' '+Q('n0976','CNBC reported that July retail-sales and industrial-output growth fell short of expectations.')+' Those earlier monthly releases still frame the demand question. Production, retail activity and purchasing intentions should eventually reinforce one another in a durable recovery. Until they do, companies must be assessed on the particular customer, product and pricing environment they face. A strong technology franchise can grow in a weak aggregate economy, while a commodity producer or discretionary retailer may still struggle. Avoid using a single macro label to erase these differences.'],
    ['Credit Impulse',Q('n0939','The Wall Street Journal reported an unexpected decline in new yuan loans.')+' Cash moving into equities is not equivalent to a sustained increase in productive borrowing. A borrower must see a return worth pursuing before lower financing costs can create new investment. Refinancing can improve survival, but it may leave demand unchanged. The stronger confirmation would involve private companies committing to commercially attractive expansion, households showing greater confidence in future income and lenders seeing viable opportunities rather than only policy targets. Equity exposure should remain tilted toward companies that can fund themselves while that transmission is incomplete.'],
    ['Property',Q('n1600','The South China Morning Post reported Shanghai easing property rules to support its sluggish housing market.')+' The measure changes the opportunity set for transactions, but the response of buyers is the decisive variable. Households weigh employment, income, prices and confidence in delivery as well as formal purchase restrictions. A developer can receive relief without regaining the ability to grow profitably. Separate the value of avoiding a disorderly deterioration from the much stronger claim that the previous property model is returning. The investable evidence would be healthier collections, completed homes and less dependence on discounting to generate activity.'],
    ['Fiscal, Policy & Trade',Q('n1521','CNBC reported Trump threatening tariffs if China restricted magnet exports.')+' This is a prospective trade risk, not a completed increase in duties. It shows why companies cannot plan solely around the existence of a temporary truce. Critical inputs and export permissions can become bargaining instruments, affecting inventory, sourcing and customer commitments. Prefer firms with flexibility and a clear ability to protect margins under different outcomes. Domestic policy can offset some uncertainty, but the effectiveness of spending depends on the quality of funded projects and the firms receiving the orders. Keep export-sensitive positions sized for an interruption in the negotiating narrative.'],
    ['Markets & Flows',p('^HSI',(1,20))+' '+p('000001.SS',(1,20))+' '+p('ASHR',(1,20))+' '+p('KWEB',(1,20))+' '+p('CNY=X',(1,20))+' The market’s strength warrants attention, particularly where it broadens beyond a single theme. It does not remove the need to assess valuation after the rally. Mainland and offshore instruments carry different sector composition, currency exposure and investor bases. Choose them to express a specific earnings or allocation view, and avoid mistaking an ETF price increase for a measured inflow.'],
    ['New / Most Important',Q('n1549','Bloomberg reported falling sales at hotpot chain Haidilao as diners held back.')+' That company-level demand warning deserves a place alongside the stronger equity narrative. A household can buy shares while remaining careful about discretionary spending. The distinction matters for companies whose valuation assumes that wealth effects will quickly become revenue. Prefer evidence of improved customer behaviour, margins and cash conversion before adding broad consumer beta. The potential opportunity is a gradual transmission from confidence into spending; the risk is that the market capitalises that transmission before businesses experience it.'],
    ['Playbook ✓','Hold a measured position in profitable platforms and diversified mainland exposure, with additions conditional on earnings delivery. Avoid an unqualified property recovery bet and keep trade-sensitive businesses diversified. Add when stronger financial confidence is matched by genuine borrowing and spending; trim when a narrow speculative rally substitutes for broader operating improvement. The right risk budget leaves room for both a further liquidity-led advance and a disappointment in demand. ⚠ Divergence: a strong stock market alongside cautious diners and weak new borrowing would show that household risk-taking and household consumption are moving on different tracks.']]),
    G('JP','Mixed','wage pressure / global rate shift',[
    ['Macro Stance',Q('n4230','The Japan Times reported Ueda expecting labour-market tightness to keep pressure on wages.')+' That supports the case for continued policy normalisation, but the pace must be assessed alongside household spending and the external environment. A global shift toward easier policy can change the currency backdrop even when Japan’s domestic wages point toward tighter conditions. The attractive companies are those able to improve profitability through pricing, productivity and capital discipline, rather than relying on an indefinitely favourable exchange rate.'],
    ['Activity & Currency',Q('n4203','CNBC reported July core inflation above expectations while noting a slower pace and easing rice-price pressure.')+' '+p('^N225',(1,20))+' '+p('JPY=X',(1,20))+' The inflation mix matters because households respond to actual purchasing power, not just to a positive nominal wage headline. Companies selling domestically need enough real spending strength to support volumes. Exporters face a separate test through foreign demand and currency translation. Keep these earnings channels distinct when comparing otherwise similar valuations.'],
    ['Playbook ✓','Balance domestic cash generators with exporters that can withstand currency volatility. Add where a company’s operating improvement survives a less helpful yen, and trim where the investment case depends mainly on translation. A foreign investor should make an explicit decision about hedging rather than inheriting a large currency wager by accident. Turn more constructive if wages, spending and margins reinforce each other; reduce broad exposure if normalisation raises financing pressure before domestic demand is ready to absorb it.']]),
    G('AU','Mixed','housing stimulus / affordability constraint',[
    ['Macro Stance',Q('n0148','CNBC reported the August Australian rate cut alongside a reduced growth forecast.')+' The combination contains both opportunity and caution. Lower borrowing costs can support household cash flow, but the reason for easing still matters. For equity selection, favour businesses whose demand can improve without requiring households to assume a much larger debt burden. Banks, retailers and construction suppliers have related but different sensitivities to that adjustment.'],
    ['Demand & Financing',Q('n0459','ABC reported concern that the home-deposit scheme could lift house prices faster than Treasury projections.')+' '+p('^AXJO',(1,20))+' '+p('AUDUSD=X',(1,20))+' A demand subsidy can improve access for a buyer while also raising the price paid if supply cannot respond. That is why approvals, construction capacity and the delivery of new housing matter alongside financing policy. Resource businesses should still be analysed through their own assets, costs and project risks.'],
    ['Playbook ✓','Prefer disciplined lenders and companies with funded, deliverable projects. Add housing-linked exposure when increased activity reaches orders and cash generation, rather than simply when policy makes borrowing easier. Reduce if affordability deteriorates while households become more financially stretched. Keep resource exposure selective and avoid treating the Australian index as a single position in either China or the domestic consumer. A balanced allocation should survive a different path for commodity earnings and household spending.']]),
    G('PL','Bearish','tax uncertainty / rebound discipline',[
    ['Macro Stance',Q('n4536','Money.pl reported a marked decline in Polish inflation.')+' '+Q('n4516','Bankier linked faster GDP growth to private consumption.')+' That domestic backdrop offers genuine support for business activity, but investors still need to ask how the resulting profit is divided. A bank-heavy index can lag an improving economy when fiscal measures change shareholder earnings. The question is therefore more specific than whether Poland is growing: which listed companies retain the benefit, which face a new burden and what price compensates for that difference? Keep the country allocation selective while bank-tax uncertainty is absorbed.'],
    ['Markets',p('PLN=X',(1,20))+' '+p('EURPLN=X',(1,20))+' '+p('ETFBW20TR.WA',(1,20))+' '+p('PKO.WA',(1,20))+' '+p('PEO.WA',(1,20))+' '+p('LPP.WA',(1,20))+' The rebound is useful as evidence that buyers are willing to revisit prices after the shock, but it does not establish the final earnings impact. The different paths of banks and consumer businesses reinforce the case for selection rather than a uniform country trade.'],
    ['Fiscal & Politics',Q('n4332','The Wall Street Journal reported plans to raise the tax rate paid by Polish banks.')+' '+Q('n4354','Notes from Poland reported the president vetoing legislation that extended support for Ukrainian refugees.')+' These are separate policy questions, but both make implementation and institutional negotiation important to the economic outlook. Avoid assuming that a proposal moves smoothly into a final outcome, or that a political disagreement affects every industry equally. For investors, the useful work is to map the cash-flow exposure: who bears a tax, who finances a programme and whose customer demand might change. Preserve flexibility until the relevant terms become clearer.'],
    ['Corporate & Sectors',Q('n4730','Bankier reported Dino preparing for a faster pace of future store openings.')+' '+Q('n4828','Strefa Inwestorów reviewed the trailers, demonstrations and release plans shown by Warsaw-listed games companies at Gamescom.')+' '+Q('n4567','Parkiet reported KGHM advancing its Retków mining investment.')+' These are different forms of future value creation. Store expansion needs attractive economics and execution; games need customers willing to pay for the finished product; mining investment needs delivery at a cost that preserves returns. Do not treat an expanded plan or a successful showcase as booked earnings. Prefer companies that connect the announcement to funded activity, customer uptake and cash generation.'],
    ['Geopolitics & Security',Q('n4344','Bloomberg reported Poland buying a stake in Finnish surveillance-satellite company Iceye.')+' '+Q('n4328','Notes from Poland reported planned Dutch troop and Patriot-system deployments in Poland.')+' Security investment has an economic role beyond a short-lived market headline. It can support specialist suppliers and infrastructure, while also competing for public funds. The investment case is strongest where strategic need meets a funded contract and a company capable of delivery. A broad defence narrative should not replace a proper assessment of ownership, valuation, procurement risk and the time before cash arrives. Funding visibility also matters to private suppliers whose own payroll and investment commitments begin before the public customer settles its bills.'],
    ['New / Most Important',Q('n4834','Business Insider Polska reported the Warsaw market recovering part of its losses at the start of the week.')+' '+Q('n4726','Bankier warned that the proposed tax could reduce bank profits and valuations.')+' The rebound and the earnings warning should be read together. A tactical recovery can begin before investors agree on a durable valuation. That makes it a poor moment to treat a bounce as proof that the fundamental issue has disappeared. Watch whether the new earnings assumptions stabilise and whether the market can distinguish better-capitalised lenders from those with less flexibility.'],
    ['Playbook ✓','Keep bank exposure below a normal strategic weight until the fiscal range and its transmission to profits are more predictable. Use consumer, software and selected industrial businesses for a domestic-demand view where their own execution supports it. Add broad-market exposure only when bank prices and earnings estimates stabilise together; reduce tactical positions if a relief rally runs ahead of the underlying repair. Maintain explicit currency limits for foreign portfolios. ⚠ Divergence: recovering share prices while the likely earnings burden remains unresolved would signal a trading bounce rather than a completed reassessment of shareholder value.']])]

def sectors():
    rows=[
    ('XLK','Mixed',
    Q('n2798','Bloomberg reported rising investor scrutiny of software businesses vulnerable to AI disruption.')+' The same technology that expands one vendor’s opportunity can make another vendor’s existing subscription less useful. Select for a durable customer problem, proprietary value and a route to profitable deployment. '+p('XLK',(1,20)),
    Q('n2475','CNBC reported Palo Alto Networks beating earnings expectations.')+' Security provides a useful commercial test: customers already have a reason to protect their systems, so better tools can enter an established spending category. Strong results still need to be assessed against contract quality and sales concessions.',
    Q('n6572','Yahoo Finance reported Databricks planning to acquire Tecton to strengthen AI-agent capabilities.')+' The watchlist is about useful functionality, rather than an acquisition label. Watch whether product integration makes deployment easier and customer value more measurable, while preserving a sensible cost of acquisition and support.',
    'A software company can use AI successfully and still lose pricing power if customers need fewer licences or cheaper alternatives improve. Trim vendors that cannot defend the economic value of their product. Increase exposure when customer retention and cash generation strengthen together, even if the marketing narrative is less dramatic.'),
    ('XLC','Bullish',
    'Platforms with a profitable advertising engine have flexibility that speculative infrastructure ventures lack. They can fund experimentation while measuring whether users and advertisers receive more value. The risk is allowing that flexibility to become an excuse for weak investment discipline. '+p('XLC',(1,20)),
    Q('n2608','Fortune highlighted the tension between Meta’s superintelligence ambitions and shareholders’ demand for advertising revenue.')+' The advertising business is the financing anchor. A company’s research goals should therefore be judged alongside the health of the franchise that pays for them, rather than as a separate source of unlimited value.',
    'Watch whether improved recommendations, ad targeting or customer tools increase the value delivered per commercial relationship. Better returns for advertisers can support pricing without depending entirely on more advertising volume. Preserve exposure where operating cash funds the buildout and where management remains willing to redirect spending when economics disappoint.',
    'The counter-signal would be growing engagement with little improvement in monetisation, accompanied by escalating fixed costs. A large audience is valuable only when it can support an attractive business. Reduce if the next phase of investment requires investors to ignore a weakening current franchise.'),
    ('XLF','Mixed',
    'The rate-cut narrative now has to share attention with policy-credibility risk. Lenders benefit from predictable funding and viable customers; they do not require every rate to move lower. Keep a preference for diversified revenue and conservative credit decisions. '+p('XLF',(1,20)),
    Q('n6562','The Dallas Fed emphasised the importance of community banks to the resilience of its regional economy.')+' That highlights the transmission channel: bank health matters because it governs the availability of credit to businesses that cannot simply issue public securities when conditions change.',
    'The earnings opportunity is strongest where deposit costs can adjust without losing important relationships, and where loan demand remains commercially attractive. Watch fee businesses and efficient operators whose returns do not rely on rapid balance-sheet expansion. A slightly slower lender can still produce a superior shareholder outcome if it avoids poor underwriting.',
    'Pressure for easier monetary policy can coexist with higher long-term risk compensation. If financing volatility rises, the apparent curve benefit may be offset by weaker credit or unstable funding. Keep bank positions smaller where the investment case assumes a smooth policy path, and cut when repayment concerns start replacing rate concerns.'),
    ('XLE','Mixed',
    'Energy should be built from the barrel, the contract and the balance sheet upward. A political disagreement can redirect flows without removing supply, while a refinery can suffer even when a producer benefits. Diversify the mechanism behind the exposure. '+p('XLE',(1,20)),
    Q('n1281','Bloomberg reported weaker Sinopec first-half profit in a lower-oil-price environment.')+' A large integrated franchise is therefore not insulated from price and margin pressure. Assess the contribution of each business rather than assuming scale guarantees resilience throughout the commodity cycle.',
    Q('n3955','CNBC reported India and Russia seeking stronger trade ties despite US pressure linked to oil.')+' Watch suppliers able to adapt logistics and customer relationships without surrendering too much margin. The upside should come from operating flexibility and disciplined capital allocation, rather than a prediction about a single diplomatic outcome.',
    'Higher crude can improve upstream revenue while hurting downstream customers and household demand. Add a producer only when its cost structure and investment plan support cash generation. Reduce policy-sensitive exposure if the geopolitical premium fades before company-level efficiencies can compensate.'),
    ('XLI','Bullish',
    'Infrastructure and aerospace remain attractive where demand is funded and contracts protect the supplier. The relevant distinction is between announcing a strategic ambition and scheduling work that a factory can deliver profitably. Execution is the scarce capability. '+p('XLI',(1,20)),
    Q('n2254','Reuters reported a larger expected tariff burden at Deere after quarterly profit declined.')+' Input and trade costs can damage an otherwise valuable franchise. For industrial portfolios, that argues for identifying the contractual ability to reprice, the source of components and the scope to change production.',
    Q('n5886','Bloomberg described pending Chinese aircraft deals as a potential advantage for Boeing and Airbus.')+' Treat negotiations as an opportunity to monitor, not booked revenue. Suppliers become more attractive when commitments are funded and production schedules can expand without recurring disruption or working-capital stress.',
    'Fast order growth is less valuable if it produces unprofitable deliveries. A fixed-price obligation can become a burden when wages and materials rise. Add companies that demonstrate reliable throughput and collections; reduce those whose promotional backlog keeps expanding while cash conversion gets worse.'),
    ('XLY','Mixed',
    'The consumer is making choices between sellers rather than voting uniformly for or against spending. Customer value, convenience and product relevance can shift market share while overall demand remains restrained. Keep that competitive dimension central. '+p('XLY',(1,20)),
    Q('n2625','CNBC reported declining sales at Target as it appointed a new chief executive, with the shares falling.')+' A leadership change supplies a possible repair path, but the key commercial evidence is whether customers return and whether inventories can be sold without deeper markdowns.',
    Q('n8064','The New York Times reported builders using more creative approaches as housing demand weakened.')+' Look for businesses able to convert demand without offering away the margin. Financing relief is useful, but a household still needs enough confidence and income to commit to a costly purchase.',
    'A volume increase bought through incentives may not improve shareholder earnings. Prefer evidence of improving transactions with stable economics, and avoid a recovery thesis based entirely on lower borrowing costs. Trim if customer interest remains weak after the seller makes the offer more generous.'),
    ('XLP','Mixed',
    'Essential demand favours reliable franchises, but investors can still overpay for resilience. The best defensive businesses make a constrained customer budget go further while protecting their own margins. That value proposition is stronger than a general safety label. '+p('XLP',(1,20)),
    Q('n0524','The Wall Street Journal described Walmart gaining shoppers while tariffs pushed prices higher.')+' More traffic can be an important competitive advantage, but the profit outcome also depends on merchandise mix, fulfilment and purchasing efficiency. A stronger customer franchise is the starting point for valuation, not the end of it.',
    'Watch the combination of recurring visits, efficient inventory and an ability to negotiate costs. An earnings surprise can emerge from better operations even when the consumer remains cautious. Prefer companies whose value offer improves retention without requiring continuous promotional spending or a deterioration in service quality.',
    'If the market broadens successfully, defensive valuations can compress despite stable business results. Size the position for that possibility. Add when the price offers a reasonable return for durable cash generation, and reduce when a safety premium becomes more important than the company’s actual capacity to grow earnings.'),
    ('XLV','Mixed',
    'The market for useful medicines can expand while the valuation of a leading producer becomes harder to defend. Clinical progress, patient access and manufacturing are different constraints. A health-care allocation should diversify those risks rather than rely on a single therapeutic story. '+p('XLV',(1,20)),
    Q('n6488','CNBC argued that Lilly’s oral obesity treatment remained a credible competitor despite data that disappointed investors.')+' The result illustrates the gap between a commercially useful medicine and an outcome that exceeds a demanding share-price expectation. A disappointing immediate reaction does not by itself answer the medical or commercial question.',
    'Monitor evidence that access, capacity and patient demand can convert an approved or promising treatment into durable revenue. The opportunity is better when adoption does not require every assumption to be favourable. Cash-generative franchises offer more room to manage setbacks than businesses dependent on one milestone.',
    'A broad defensive-sector trade can conceal concentrated clinical exposure. Cut risk where the valuation assumes an uncomplicated path from a study to widespread profitable use. Become more constructive when the remaining commercial hurdles are understood and the share price compensates for them.'),
    ('XLB','Mixed',
    'Supply, customer demand and operating delivery need separate treatment in materials. A commodity can rise because a project stops, even though the owner of that project is worse off. Copper’s electrical uses deserve their own asset-level analysis. '+p('XLB',(1,20)),
    Q('n2721','Bloomberg reported Codelco cutting copper guidance after an accident disrupted its recovery.')+' The operational reminder is direct: investors receive company cash flow, not the chart of the metal it produces. Safety, availability and costs can change the earnings outcome even when customers still need the product.',
    Q('n0469','Mining.com reported iron ore strengthening after a fatal incident halted Rio Tinto’s Simandou project.')+' That is a supply development in a different commodity, not proof of broad demand acceleration. For copper exposure, prefer planned production meeting funded grid and computing investment, with realistic capital budgets.',
    'A higher commodity price can encourage costly expansion and inflate supplier charges. Add a producer when better revenue reaches cash generation; reduce when execution disappointments absorb the price benefit. Keep miners with different operating constraints separate rather than assigning them an identical cyclical thesis.'),
    ('XLRE','Mixed',
    'Property valuation can respond quickly to rate expectations, while rents, occupancy and debt maturity adjust more slowly. The gap between those clocks creates both opportunity and risk. Prefer income that can carry financing obligations through an imperfect recovery. '+p('XLRE',(1,20)),
    Q('n5917','Business Wire announced an agreement for Morgan Properties to acquire Dream Residential REIT.')+' A specific buyer and transaction can clarify the value of particular assets. The result cannot be transferred automatically to offices, industrial space or landlords with a different financing structure.',
    'Look for an improving operating trajectory combined with manageable maturities. The best setup is a landlord whose tenants remain healthy just as refinancing pressure eases. Avoid requiring a large asset revaluation to justify distributions or to make the balance sheet appear sustainable.',
    'Stimulus can raise bids for assets before it improves the tenants paying rent. A property stock that rallies while operating income deteriorates deserves a tighter risk limit. Add when occupancy and collections confirm the financing story; trim if the distribution increasingly depends on borrowing or asset sales.'),
    ('XLU','Bullish',
    'Electricity demand is an investment opportunity only when the asset owner can earn an adequate return on the capacity it builds. The projects need permits, fuel, interconnection and financing before the revenue arrives. That favours practical delivery. '+p('XLU',(1,20)),
    Q('n5888','Utility Dive reported Black Hills and Northwestern agreeing to merge with data-centre demand in view.')+' The strategic logic brings attention to generation and networks, but the shareholder case still depends on integration, financing and the allowed or contracted return on new investment.',
    Q('n6544','Yahoo Finance examined the vast prospective power consumption of a Wyoming data centre.')+' Watch companies that can turn such demand into funded connection work and viable contracts. A project’s enormous size should increase scrutiny of its funding and timing, rather than make those questions feel secondary.',
    'The electricity customer can have a strong balance sheet while the utility still earns a disappointing return on serving it. Stay constructive where customer commitments and regulatory treatment protect economics. Reduce where construction spending runs ahead of recovery or where demand forecasts require repeated upward revisions to justify valuation.'),
    ('SXAP','Bearish',
    'Auto manufacturers need to improve competitive position while navigating tariffs, product changes and financing-sensitive customers. Those pressures do not disappear because the broader market becomes more optimistic about rates. Keep a demanding hurdle for a turnaround allocation. '+p('EXV5.DE',(1,20)),
    Q('n6549','CNBC described automakers confronting difficult realities amid overlapping crises.')+' The operational work involves cost, model mix, pricing and regional exposure. A company that improves one area can still disappoint if another consumes the benefit, particularly when production capacity is expensive to adjust.',
    Q('n3963','Automotive News discussed possible mutual recognition of US and EU vehicle standards.')+' Simpler rules could reduce friction, but the proposal does not guarantee better demand or a successful product. Watch cash generation and customer response before capitalising a regulatory benefit into a much larger earnings recovery.',
    'Short-covering and relief can generate a convincing rebound without repairing the franchise. Use strength to reduce structurally weak exposure until volumes, prices and costs begin to align. Turn more constructive only when operating evidence supports a valuation that does not require every political development to be favourable.'),
    ('SOXX','Mixed',
    'The semiconductor portfolio now needs a distinction between demand beneficiaries and stocks priced for an exceptional announcement. Computing demand may remain attractive even if a near-term event disappoints. Avoid using one company’s valuation to decide the entire supply-chain allocation. '+p('SOXX',(1,20)),
    Q('n2577','Reuters reported Analog Devices forecasting better results on strong industrial demand.')+' That offers a different demand channel from large AI deployments. A broader industrial order improvement could support utilisation and margins across less celebrated parts of the semiconductor complex.',
    Q('n2800','Yahoo Finance reported Broadcom gaining after UBS lifted its target on Google AI-chip demand.')+' '+Q('n2827','CNBC highlighted Nvidia’s demanding earnings expectations.')+' Customer-specific opportunities are useful, but analyst enthusiasm should be treated as a higher hurdle rather than as a delivered result.',
    'A company can beat a conventional forecast and still disappoint investors who have already raised the unofficial bar. Keep single-event positions contained and prefer a supply-chain mix with multiple customer engines. Add after delivered results and a durable market response; reduce if the price relies on progressively more optimistic targets.')]
    labels=['Narrative','Reported','EPS Upside Watch','⚡ Breaking Convention']
    return [{'key':key,'stance':stance,'parts':list(zip(labels,texts))} for key,stance,*texts in rows]

def earnings():
    return B('A beat clears the accounting hurdle; the outlook clears the valuation hurdle',[
    ['Rewarded',Q('n2535','CNBC reported Home Depot shares rising after the company maintained its full-year forecast.')+' The lesson is that investors can reward a credible floor when they have been worried about further deterioration. A stable outlook can be more valuable than an impressive growth label if it gives a portfolio a clearer range of future cash flows. The demand behind the result matters: a company should be able to hold its customers without consuming too much margin or capital to do so.'],
    ['Punished',Q('n2736','Yahoo Finance reported Intuit falling after a quarterly beat because its annual forecast was cautious.')+' '+Q('n2701','Yahoo Finance reported Walmart falling when its profit outlook missed forecasts despite stronger US sales growth.')+' Neither reaction says that a good business has become useless. Both show that the share price makes a promise about the future. A past result can satisfy an accounting comparison while the outlook fails the promise investors were actually paying for.'],
    ['Pattern',Q('n2624','Yahoo Finance reported Target beating low earnings expectations while its shares declined.')+' A low formal forecast is therefore an unreliable protection by itself. The market also judges customer momentum, leadership, costs and the plausibility of a repair. Compare the direction of the business with the expectation embedded in the valuation, rather than sorting companies into a simple beat-or-miss table. A company gaining credibility can deserve an addition after the event, while one losing credibility can remain unattractive after a large decline.'],
    ['Attention into EPS',Q('n2783','MarketWatch contrasted low expectations for retailers with increasingly demanding expectations for Nvidia.')+' This is where attention becomes a risk variable. The more investors focus on a single success story, the less useful a conventional forecast may be as a guide to the immediate reaction. Customer demand must become delivered revenue and profit, and the stock must still offer a return for ordinary execution. A popular narrative can widen awareness while narrowing the margin for error.'],
    ['Playbook','Set the event position according to the gap between demonstrated economics and market expectations. Retain a core in strong businesses, hedge concentrated announcements and add when a result improves the forward profit path without requiring a more extravagant valuation. Cut when a company needs another optimistic explanation to reconcile customer behaviour with its forecast. The opportunity lies in identifying where credibility is improving faster than the price, rather than in predicting every first-session reaction.']])

def underowned():
    return [
    B('The financing layer of physical AI infrastructure',[
    ['Attention Gap',Q('n3575','Bloomberg projected data centres helping drive a larger infrastructure-securitisation market.')+' The financing architecture deserves as much analysis as the demand forecast. Long-lived assets need a dependable match between customer payments, debt service and the schedule on which capacity becomes useful.'],
    ['Exposure & Risk','Monitor liquid electrical-equipment and infrastructure suppliers such as Eaton and Quanta rather than reaching automatically for a new financing wrapper. Suppliers still face working-capital and customer-concentration risk, but the source of their revenue can be easier to identify than the equity economics of a heavily financed asset owner.'],
    ['Trigger to Watch','The confirmation is a funded customer commitment becoming equipment deliveries and collections. Add when cash conversion holds as orders expand. Reduce if the project’s financial structure becomes more complex while the timing of actual customer revenue moves further away.']]),
    B('Institutional digital-asset use beyond the token target',[
    ['Attention Gap',Q('n1829','The Block reported DBS planning tokenised structured notes on Ethereum for institutional investors.')+' A concrete use case is more informative than another distant token-price target. It creates a commercial question about settlement, distribution and service revenue that can be analysed separately from speculative price momentum.'],
    ['Exposure & Risk','Treat the token and the financial institution as different exposures. Direct Ether carries asset-price and liquidity risk; a service provider depends on fee economics, compliance and customer adoption. Avoid assuming that greater network use must translate mechanically into a proportionate return for every security associated with it.'],
    ['Trigger to Watch','Watch actual adoption, repeat transactions and commercially useful fee generation. Add only when the chosen instrument captures the value being created. Reduce if attention migrates from customer usage to increasingly elaborate corporate treasury structures with uncertain benefits for existing shareholders.']]),
    B('Japanese investment discipline behind the AI enthusiasm',[
    ['Attention Gap',Q('n4251','Nikkei Asia asked whether SoftBank’s AI investments would pay off after its participation in the technology rally.')+' The valuable question is capital allocation: who commits money, on what terms, and how long shareholders must wait before an investment becomes cash rather than an attractive valuation mark.'],
    ['Exposure & Risk','Use diversified Japanese equities for broader earnings exposure and treat SoftBank as a separate investment-risk position. An investment company combines asset valuations, financing and management decisions; it does not provide the same economic claim as a profitable operating supplier. Currency exposure adds another independent source of volatility.'],
    ['Trigger to Watch','Increase exposure when investment gains are supported by durable customer economics and a sensible funding structure. Avoid adding merely because a private valuation rises. The theme improves when capital discipline becomes visible alongside strategic ambition, and weakens when funding commitments outgrow financial flexibility.']]),
    B('Satellite infrastructure needs deployment, not just a countdown',[
    ['Attention Gap',Q('n5186','Yahoo Finance examined AST SpaceMobile’s planned satellite deployment and its possible investment implications.')+' The attractive angle is the gap between an understandable customer need and the difficult work required to provide it. A compelling service promise becomes valuable only through reliable deployment and commercial delivery.'],
    ['Exposure & Risk','Keep AST SpaceMobile as a tightly sized satellite allocation, with diversified aerospace exposure available for investors seeking a less concentrated route. Funding, launch, technical performance and customer commitments can each interrupt the path to cash generation. None should be treated as an incidental detail.'],
    ['Trigger to Watch','Look for delivery against the stated plan and a credible link from capacity to paying customers. Add after execution reduces uncertainty, rather than solely ahead of a promotional milestone. Reduce if financing needs expand without a matching improvement in commercial visibility.']])]

def crypto():
    return B('The drawdown tests whether ownership is investment or financing',[
    ['Market Context',p('BTC-USD',(1,20))+' '+p('ETH-USD',(1,20))+' '+p('SOL-USD',(1,20))+' The latest completed day is a reminder that a strong longer-term narrative can coexist with a sharp immediate loss. For leveraged holders, the path matters because they may not be able to remain invested long enough for the thesis to recover.'],
    ['New / Most Important',Q('n2001','Bloomberg reported biotechnology companies turning to digital coins in an effort to lift their share prices.')+' That is a capital-allocation question as well as a crypto story. Buying a token can change the risk of a listed company without improving the economics of its original business. '+Q('n1998','Yahoo Finance reported AUSTRAC ordering an audit of Binance Australia over anti-money-laundering concerns.')+' Compliance, custody and access therefore remain part of the instrument choice, even when attention is focused on the market direction.'],
    ['Playbook','Reduce leverage before trying to identify the precise bottom of a volatile move. Retain only the directional exposure that the portfolio can hold through a further drawdown, and choose a vehicle whose costs and economic claim are clear. A company owning tokens must create value per share after funding and management decisions; the headline size of a treasury is insufficient. Rebuild risk when price stability and dependable demand replace forced selling, and avoid switching into a more complex wrapper merely because it appears to offer a larger rebound. A disciplined smaller position leaves room to exploit an opportunity without relying on a perfectly timed recovery.']])

def flows():
    return B('Credibility, collateral and the cost of keeping a position',[
    ['Global Liquidity',Q('n8384','CNBC reported Trump telling Lisa Cook she was removed, while Cook disputed his authority to do so.')+' The attempted action introduces an unresolved institutional question. Investors should distinguish the political demand for lower rates from the financing conditions that markets actually deliver. If confidence in inflation management weakens, longer-term debt can require more compensation even when the expected policy path falls. That would matter to housing, property, infrastructure and leveraged equity positions. Preserve the ability to adjust rather than betting the portfolio on a legal conclusion. A credible central bank can support financial stability through changing conditions; uncertainty about its independence can make the transmission less predictable.'],
    ['Rates & Dollar',p('DX-Y.NYB',(1,20))+' '+p('TLT',(1,20))+' '+p('HYG',(1,20))+' '+p('LQD',(1,20))+' These prices do not describe a uniform flight toward risk or safety. Dollar and duration exposure can move against a portfolio that assumes an effortless continuation of the easing rally. Credit ETFs also contain rate exposure, so their movements should not be described as measured spread changes. Keep government-duration risk, corporate-credit risk and currency risk in separate limits. That makes it possible to retain a hedge without accidentally increasing the same financing sensitivity already embedded in property or growth stocks.'],
    ['Credit Check',Q('n6553','Bloomberg reported BlackRock pausing fundraising for its latest Asia private-credit fund.')+' This is a specific fundraising development, rather than proof of a universal credit squeeze. It nevertheless reinforces the value of distinguishing capital that is promised, capital that is available and capital already committed. A business requiring another favourable financing round carries a different risk from one paying for expansion from operations. In the public portfolio, favour borrowers with time and flexibility, and demand a stronger return from companies whose investment case depends on refinancing on unusually attractive terms. Liquidity can look ample in an index while a particular borrower faces a difficult negotiation.'],
    ['Equity & Fund Flows',Q('n3605','The Wall Street Journal examined record margin debt and what it meant for the equity market.')+' Leverage changes the response to ordinary volatility. A holder funding a position may need to sell when prices fall, even if the long-run argument remains intact. That can make a crowded theme more fragile than a simple ownership count suggests. '+Q('n4002','Bloomberg reported Canadians adding US stocks despite the trade dispute.')+' Cross-border interest can support markets without removing concentration risk. Use flow and financing information to understand the potential marginal buyer or seller, then judge whether the underlying asset still offers an adequate return.'],
    ['Portfolio Implication','Keep a liquid core and reduce overlapping claims on the same favourable funding scenario. A property stock, a crypto treasury and a speculative technology company may appear diversified by sector while all depend on cheap capital and patient investors. Finance new ideas by trimming those overlaps. Hold a measured gold allocation and liquid duration for different adverse scenarios, recognising that they can behave differently when inflation credibility is questioned. Add equity risk when price action, credit and operating guidance agree; reduce when they diverge. The objective is to stay able to act after volatility rises, rather than to maximise exposure at the moment financing feels easiest.']])

def anticipatory():
    return [
    B('The Nvidia event: the demand thesis meets the expectation bar',[
    ['What Is Priced',Q('n0520','Yahoo Finance examined Nvidia ahead of its Aug. 27 earnings report.')+' The market has a clear event to focus on, and a substantial part of the wider technology narrative depends on how investors interpret it. A strong long-run business case does not settle the return on a short-dated position.'],
    ['Conditional Expression','Retain diversified semiconductor exposure and hedge an oversized single-name event position. Add when the actual earnings path improves enough to justify the valuation and the market sustains that interpretation. If an apparently strong announcement cannot retain buying interest, allow the adjustment to develop before committing more risk.'],
    ['Risk','High expectations can make a good report feel ordinary. Export policy and product transitions also affect the quality of future demand. Avoid translating an analyst target into a result, or using confidence in AI adoption to dismiss a weaker company-level profit outlook.']]),
    B('Federal Reserve governance: lower rates versus higher risk compensation',[
    ['What Is Priced',Q('n8383','NPR described the attempted removal of Lisa Cook and the prospect of legal conflict.')+' The outcome remains open. The economic risk is that pressure for easier policy changes investors’ confidence in the future purchasing power of money, rather than merely changing a single meeting’s rate expectation.'],
    ['Conditional Expression','Keep duration exposure moderate and diversify the defensive book. Add rate-sensitive equities only when credit and long-term financing conditions remain supportive. If longer yields rise while policy expectations fall, reduce the most leveraged beneficiaries of the easing story and favour internally funded businesses.'],
    ['Risk','Political headlines can generate rapid reversals while legal and institutional processes evolve. Do not size the position around certainty about an unresolved outcome. The relevant market confirmation is how financing terms and inflation expectations respond, rather than the immediate tone of a statement.']]),
    B('Polish monetary easing: borrower benefit versus bank earnings',[
    ['What Is Priced',Q('n4864','Strefa Inwestorów examined rate forecasts ahead of the September Monetary Policy Council meeting.')+' Lower inflation creates a discussion about relief, but the equity effect differs between a household borrower, a retailer and a lender. The bank-tax debate makes that distribution especially important.'],
    ['Conditional Expression','Express an improving domestic-demand view through companies whose own margins and customer activity support it. Keep a smaller bank allocation until both the interest-income and fiscal assumptions are clearer. Add lenders only when earnings estimates stabilise and the valuation compensates for the remaining uncertainty.'],
    ['Risk','A policy move can help economic activity while reducing a particular sector’s near-term profits. Conversely, an expected cut can already be reflected in the price. Avoid confusing a valid macro argument with an automatic earnings catalyst for every stock in the country index. Track borrower relief and shareholder profit as separate outcomes of the same decision.']]),
    B('China’s equity wealth effect: savings must become customers',[
    ['What Is Priced',Q('n1552','CNBC linked household savings to the Chinese equity rally.')+' The constructive scenario is that financial confidence eventually supports spending and productive investment. The weaker scenario is a rotation between financial assets while customers remain cautious and private borrowing demand stays soft.'],
    ['Conditional Expression','Own profitable liquid exposure in stages and look for companies converting customer interest into margins and cash. Add broad consumer beta only when operating results corroborate the wealth-effect story. Reduce speculative positions if equity leadership narrows while real-economy demand continues to disappoint.'],
    ['Risk','Financial confidence can turn quickly when a rally depends on price appreciation as its own justification. Trade restrictions or disappointing earnings can interrupt the feedback loop. Keep property and highly leveraged businesses separate from the more resilient franchises within the same market. A changing valuation does not resolve an underlying cash-flow problem.']])]

def catalysts():
    return [
    B('$NVDA — wait for delivery to meet a demanding valuation',[
    ['Catalyst & Thesis',Q('n2828','CNBC reported a series of favourable Nvidia endorsements ahead of earnings.')+' The immediate catalyst is a test of expectations, not a delivered result. Retain a core position in the demand engine while making the event allocation small enough to survive an unfavourable first reaction.'],
    ['Price Hurdle & Risk',p('NVDA',(5,20))+' The business must clear a higher hurdle when endorsements lift the market’s confidence. Product transitions and export permissions can also affect the quality of the forward outlook.'],
    ['Trade Expression','Hold measured exposure and hedge concentration. Add after demonstrated operating progress and a durable response; reduce if investors need increasingly optimistic targets to defend the same earnings path.']],stance='Mixed'),
    B('$AVGO — a customer-specific AI channel earns attention',[
    ['Catalyst & Thesis',Q('n2800','Yahoo Finance reported Broadcom rising as UBS increased its target on Google AI-chip demand.')+' A named customer channel is more useful than an indiscriminate chip-sector narrative. The investment case should still be judged on the revenue and profit actually captured by the supplier.'],
    ['Price Hurdle & Risk',p('AVGO',(1,20))+' An analyst upgrade can accelerate the price before the company delivers the implied improvement. Customer concentration and the economics of new business remain important sources of risk.'],
    ['Trade Expression','Accumulate selectively when valuation leaves room for delivery. Trim if demand optimism expands without a corresponding improvement in the operating outlook, or if customer-specific exposure becomes too large for the portfolio.']],stance='Bullish'),
    B('$INTC — a strategic asset still needs commercial customers',[
    ['Catalyst & Thesis',Q('n6540','The New York Times reported the US stake in Intel alongside Trump’s promise of more deals.')+' The financing relationship can alter runway and incentives, but it does not itself establish a competitive return on the next investment dollar. Keep the commercial turnaround separate from the political endorsement.'],
    ['Price Hurdle & Risk',p('INTC',(1,5))+' After a strong longer-term repricing, the stock needs operational evidence to justify continued enthusiasm. Official involvement can support strategic capacity while leaving difficult questions about execution and shareholder returns.'],
    ['Trade Expression','Use a modest tactical weight. Increase only when product delivery and customer commitments strengthen; exit a momentum position if new support announcements stop producing a durable price response.']],stance='Mixed'),
    B('$PANW — useful security tools face a commercial conversion test',[
    ['Catalyst & Thesis',Q('n2551','ET Telecom reported Palo Alto forecasts pointing to an AI boost for cybersecurity products, with a positive share reaction.')+' The opportunity is selling more useful capability into a real customer requirement. Preserve a constructive view while demanding evidence that sales quality and collections support the growth.'],
    ['Price Hurdle & Risk',p('PANW',(1,20))+' Recurring-revenue language does not remove the need to examine concessions, implementation and profitability. A broad platform can create customer value or become a complicated discounting strategy.'],
    ['Trade Expression','Buy controlled weakness when customer demand and cash generation remain intact. Reduce if future growth requires materially less attractive economics or if the investment story becomes detached from commercial delivery.']],stance='Bullish'),
    B('$DE — tariff costs make the earnings repair harder',[
    ['Catalyst & Thesis',Q('n2254','Reuters reported Deere warning of a bigger tariff impact following lower quarterly profit.')+' The near-term earnings argument faces a specific cost headwind. A durable franchise can still be a poor tactical purchase when investors underestimate how long costs take to pass through to customers.'],
    ['Price Hurdle & Risk',p('DE',(1,20))+' Financing relief may support equipment buyers, but it cannot guarantee demand or immediately repair the manufacturer’s margin. The risk to a defensive stance is a faster improvement in orders or pricing.'],
    ['Trade Expression','Underweight until order quality and cost recovery improve together. Reconsider after evidence that operating cash can recover without relying on an unusually favourable commodity or financing backdrop.']],stance='Bearish'),
    B('$WMT — winning shoppers is useful, retaining the profit is decisive',[
    ['Catalyst & Thesis',Q('n2698','CNBC reported Walmart increasing its sales and earnings outlook while tariff costs rose.')+' The customer franchise provides a foundation, but the stock’s return depends on the margin retained after sourcing, fulfilment and pricing decisions. Treat resilience as a business advantage that still needs a sensible valuation.'],
    ['Price Hurdle & Risk',p('WMT',(1,20))+' A popular defensive franchise can face a demanding profit hurdle even when customer demand is sound. Watch the conversion of sales strength into operating cash rather than focusing only on traffic.'],
    ['Trade Expression','Hold or add in stages when valuation and profit visibility align. Reduce if price increases weaken the customer proposition or if the market demands an ever larger premium for unchanged operating resilience.']],stance='Mixed')]

def retail():
    return [
    B('Ether / ETH — the record becomes a test of who can stay invested',[
    ['Why Retail Is Here',Q('n1983','Axios reported Ether breaking its old all-time high.')+' The record changes the emotional character of the trade. Holders can feel that years of waiting have been vindicated, while new buyers see a familiar asset finally catching up with a story they already understand. The latest drawdown then becomes a test of identity: is weakness a welcome chance to buy, or evidence that the market ran ahead of the argument? The attraction is the promise of a major financial network whose token also benefits from scarcity. That combines a technological mission with an easily repeated price narrative, making it particularly persuasive when a visible milestone has just been reached.'],
    ['What Is Driving It',p('ETH-USD',(1,5))+' '+p('BMNR',(1,20))+' '+p('BTC-USD',(1,5))+' '+Q('n2003','CoinDesk reported a bitcoin flash crash causing substantial Sunday liquidations while the rotation toward Ethereum continued.')+' The liquidation story and the completed price decline expose the importance of funding. A holder using cash can choose how to respond to volatility; a holder using leverage may have the decision made for them. A listed treasury company adds another layer because its share price depends on the token, financing terms and the valuation investors assign to the corporate vehicle. The instrument can therefore matter as much as the directional call.'],
    ['The Social Signal',Q('n1962','Yahoo Finance highlighted Ether near record levels and Tom Lee’s ambitious year-end price forecast.')+' '+Q('n2002','BitMine’s own PR Newswire release promoted its Ether-treasury position and the liquidity of its shares.')+' These are different kinds of attention: an investment forecast supplies a destination, while an issuer’s promotional statement supplies an accessible vehicle. Neither is a guarantee of the return available to a new buyer. The social appeal lies in turning complexity into a short instruction: the asset is scarce, powerful investors are interested and a listed stock makes participation easy. After a sharp reversal, that instruction needs to survive harder questions about entry price, borrowing and the value captured per share.'],
    ['Historical Analog','Bitcoin in 2020–2021 provides a useful mechanical comparison. An asset can acquire a larger audience when a network or adoption story meets price strength and new ways to own it. The feedback loop makes each visible gain feel like confirmation of the underlying thesis, attracting participants who would not have entered on the fundamental argument alone. Once that process is established, a decline does more than reduce wealth: it challenges the interpretation that rising prices were inevitable. The lesson for the current trade concerns funding and patience. A valid long-run adoption argument cannot protect a leveraged holder from being forced out during the path between entry and the hoped-for outcome.'],
    ['Smart Money View',Q('n1848','The Wall Street Journal described Peter Thiel among investors increasing exposure to Ether.')+' Recognisable institutional interest can lend credibility to the asset, but professionals still choose different entry points, vehicles and risk limits. The disagreement need not be about whether the network is useful. It can be about how much growth the token price already discounts, which claim captures that growth and how long a portfolio can tolerate volatility. A corporate treasury may give public-market access while introducing dilution, governance and valuation risk. Direct exposure may offer a cleaner link to the asset while requiring its own custody and liquidity decisions. The sensible question is which risk the investor intends to own, rather than which well-known name appears in the story.'],
    ['When the Narrative Breaks','The warning is a repeated failure to rebuild demand after a record or a positive adoption headline. A scarcity story also weakens when new financing vehicles proliferate faster than dependable end demand. For a listed treasury, monitor whether financing increases asset value per share after costs, rather than simply expanding the headline treasury. Another warning is a growing gap between bullish targets and the ability of the market to absorb selling. Keep any speculative position small enough to hold without borrowing and reassess if relative strength deteriorates further. The disciplined response to a sharp decline is to examine the instrument and the funding before deciding that a cheaper quote must be a better opportunity.']]),
    B('Opendoor / OPEN — the comeback meets an ordinary trading setback',[
    ['Why Retail Is Here',Q('n5123','MarketWatch described the AI shift behind Opendoor’s rally while warning buyers to be careful.')+' '+p('OPEN',(1,5))+' The appealing story remains a technology-assisted repair of a difficult housing business. After the previous surge, the new question is whether believers keep buying when the price stops supplying effortless confirmation. The setback is useful because it makes the distinction between a business thesis and a trading identity harder to avoid.'],
    ['Where It Breaks','Keep this as a short, tightly sized carryover rather than refreshing the entire comeback argument with a new target. The commercial test remains better transaction economics and cash conversion. Reduce if favourable announcements can no longer attract durable demand, or if funding terms transfer too much of the hoped-for recovery away from existing shareholders. A dramatic earlier move is a reason to manage risk, not a reason to demand that the next move must be equally dramatic.']]),
    B('Nvidia / NVDA — believers wait for the report to answer',[
    ['Why Retail Is Here',Q('n5116','Stocktwits described retail confidence in Nvidia alongside reports of plans for advanced AI-chip expansion in China.')+' '+p('NVDA',(1,20))+' The emotional hook is the belief that the leading supplier will validate the whole AI investment cycle again. A pending report gives that belief a near-term focal point, while favourable analyst commentary can make waiting feel like the only obstacle to another advance.'],
    ['Where It Breaks','An export plan is not permission, and an earnings preview is not an outcome. The trade becomes vulnerable when confidence rises faster than the result required to support the valuation. Keep event exposure separate from a long-run core position, and reduce if good operating news cannot hold its price response. The company can remain important while the short-dated trade disappoints. Product mix, customer commitments and the durability of margins still decide what that importance is worth to shareholders.']]),
    B('Gold / GLD — policy credibility becomes part of the hedge',[
    ['Why Retail Is Here',Q('n5138','CNBC examined a gold-related strategy for investors seeking protection from risk and volatility.')+' '+p('GC=F',(1,5))+' The attempted intervention in Federal Reserve governance adds an institutional dimension to an already familiar hedge. An investor can remain constructive on businesses while wanting some protection against a less predictable monetary framework. That is a portfolio purpose rather than a requirement to predict an immediate crisis.'],
    ['Where It Breaks','Gold still carries price and liquidity risk, and it can suffer when investors need to raise cash. A stronger dollar or a rise in longer yields can also challenge the entry price. Keep the allocation measured and prefer an instrument that matches the intended exposure. A mining company adds operating economics, while a bullion position does not provide an earnings stream. Reduce if the hedge becomes a dominant speculative bet that needs increasingly alarming headlines to justify its size.']])]

def main():
    spec={'date':w.date,'geo':macro(),'sectors':sectors(),'earnings_pattern':earnings(),'underowned':underowned(),
          'crypto':crypto(),'flows':flows(),'anticipatory':anticipatory(),'catalysts':catalysts(),
          'retail_intro':'Ether’s record-to-drawdown trade is the clearest crowd narrative under pressure, recalling the funding and conviction tests around Bitcoin in 2020–2021, GameStop in 2021 and the technology enthusiasm of 1999.',
          'retail':retail()}
    w.save(spec)

if __name__=='__main__':main()
